{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update.json\", \"summary\": \"Interprets receipt fd88bc508e4f413393838b7d64657137, the thirty-second observation of the blocked startup replay. The 128-batch control returned in 5 ms while the 129-batch case had still not returned after 30000 ms, with one goroutine left inside processLogs, so the blocked case outlasts a completed replay of the same shape by roughly four orders of magnitude. That converts the permanence claim from an inference resting on five-second cutoffs plus source reading into a measurement with a wide margin, and the account now says so. The rationale gains the receipt with its parsed indices, the counterevidence entry that described permanence as timeout-plus-source is rewritten to include the new measurement while keeping the source argument, and a limitation records that thirty seconds is still a finite window even though the same-shaped control finishes in milliseconds. Knowledge entries 1255b78953904846987cdc19826340c8-knowledge-0 and -1 carry the new receipt's executions for unchanged statements, and joint_history notes that it comes from a further experiment identifier that keeps the seeded boundary pair and only lengthens the window. The submission validates with zero schema errors and requests no execution.\"}"}}
